# Built binaries. Each service compiles to one at the repo root, so a plain
# `go build ./services/...` leaves them in the working tree.
#
# One entry per directory under services/, and nothing else: an entry for a
# binary that cannot be built ignores a file that would never appear, and a
# missing entry lets a real build artefact be committed. Both were true before
# the split — /sloprail and /sr-command named binaries that no longer exist and
# never existed, while sr-agent was built and unlisted.
/sr
/sr-session
/sr-guardrail
/sr-file
/sr-mark
/sr-agent

# Where `make build` puts the same six binaries. The entries above cover a bare
# `go build ./services/...`, which drops them at the root; the Makefile builds
# with -o bin/ instead, so both layouts have to be listed or whichever one is
# not gets committed.
/bin/

# Where the e2e harness builds the binary it drives. Under the git directory
# rather than the system temp dir, because macOS reaps /var/folders mid-run —
# see tests/e2e/harness/harness.go. Listed here for the case where someone
# points it at the tree instead.
/.e2e-bin/

# The session state store, and the sidecars SQLite keeps beside an open one.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
